{
  "slug": "setting-up-google-oauth-credentials-for-blogger",
  "title": "Setting Up Google OAuth Credentials for Blogger Automation",
  "description": "In this post I explained how to create a secure admin dashboard by Google OAuth credentials for an application.",
  "category": "Web Development",
  "tags": [],
  "url": "https://www.techtips.fun/blog/setting-up-google-oauth-credentials-for-blogger/",
  "theme": "github-dark",
  "durationInFrames": 930,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "kicker": "Web Development",
      "title": "Setting Up Google OAuth Credentials for Blogger Automation",
      "subtitle": "In this post I explained how to create a secure admin dashboard by Google OAuth…",
      "durationInFrames": 105
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "Web Development",
      "heading": "Before you begin make sure you have",
      "body": "A Google Account. A Google Cloud project. The web address of your application. The OAuth callback URL for your application.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "Web Development",
      "heading": "Step 1: Create or select a Google Cloud project",
      "body": "Open the Google Cloud Console. Select the project menu at the top of the page. Select an existing project.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "Web Development",
      "heading": "Step 2: Enable the Blogger API",
      "body": "Open the API Library. Search for Blogger API v3. Select Blogger API v3 from the search results. Select Enable.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "Web Development",
      "heading": "Step 3: Configure the OAuth consent screen",
      "body": "The OAuth consent screen tells users which application requests access to their Google Account.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "Web Development",
      "heading": "Configure the audience",
      "body": "Open the Audience page. Select External if people outside your Google Workspace organization will use the application.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "Web Development",
      "heading": "Add the Blogger scope",
      "body": "Open the Data Access page. Select Add or Remove Scopes. Search for the Blogger API scope. Select https://www.googleapis.com/auth/blogger.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "outro",
      "heading": "Read the full article",
      "body": "New posts every week on the blog.",
      "url": "techtips.fun",
      "durationInFrames": 105
    }
  ],
